{"name":"Retributor Armour Metal","hex":"#c39e81","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"retributor","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of retributer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retributor"},{"term":"armour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["British standard spelling of armor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["British standard spelling of armor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/armour"},{"term":"metal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Chemical elements or alloys, their ores, and the mines where their ores come from.\n Any of a number of chemical elements in the periodic table that form a metallic bond with other metal atoms; generally shiny, somewhat malleable and hard, often a conductor of heat and electricity.\n\n Any material with similar physical properties as those chemical elements, especially as a combination of several of them, such as an alloy.\n\n An element which was not directly created after the Big Bang but instead formed through nuclear reactions; any element other than hydrogen and helium.\n\n Crushed rock, stones etc. used to make a road.\n\n The ore from which a metal is derived.\n A mine from which ores are taken.","Any of a number of chemical elements in the periodic table that form a metallic bond with other metal atoms; generally shiny, somewhat malleable and hard, often a conductor of heat and electricity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterized by strong drum-beats and distorted guitars. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Having the emotional or social characteristics associated with metal music; brash, bold, frank, unyielding, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Armour","blocks":[{"text":"Armour or armor is a covering used to protect an object, individual, or vehicle from physical injury or damage, especially direct contact weapons or projectiles during combat, or from a potentially dangerous environment or activity. Personal armour is used to protect soldiers and war animals. Vehicle armour is used on warships, armoured fighting vehicles, and some combat aircraft, mostly ground attack aircraft."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Xixia_Chainmail_Armor_%2841985701161%29.jpg/330px-Xixia_Chainmail_Armor_%2841985701161%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armour"},{"title":"Metal","blocks":[{"text":"A metal is a material that, when polished or fractured, shows a lustrous appearance, and conducts electricity and heat relatively well. These properties are all associated with having electrons available at the Fermi level, as opposed to nonmetallic materials which do not. Metals are typically ductile and malleable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg/330px-Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Arms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg/500px-Arms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Arms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg/1280px-Arms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Arms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg/500px-Arms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Armour “harness”. German, about AD 1540-50. Metropolitan Museum of At","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Paris_bordone_016.jpg